Point "added to the browser" at the button the shell drew.

Installing an extension ends with a bubble pointing at the extension's
toolbar button, or at the extensions button when it has none of its own.
With the shell drawing the browser there is no Chromium toolbar to point at:
GetExtensionsContainerViews() finds nothing, and the dialog fell through to
a browser-modal box in the middle of the window.

The shell draws those buttons and already reports where they are, under the
two names Chromium's own rule distinguishes -- "extension:<id>" and
"extensions". Nothing read them: GetAuraShellAnchorRect() has been in the
bridge, with a comment describing exactly this, and no caller. This is the
caller.

The fallback order matches desktop's: the extension's own button first,
the extensions button when it is not pinned, and the modal box when the
shell has reported neither.

The rect it anchors to is logged with what it is made of -- the rect the
shell reported, the window origin it is moved by -- because the shell has
seen the bubble away from its button and from outside it cannot be told
which is off. Diagnostic; it goes once that is settled. (It lives here, not
in a later patch: a later patch changing lines this one adds stops this
one from being recognised as applied.)

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

